Fix the key names that look up nothing: Usr1, Fn+Usr1, Fn+Esc, d-pad right

pyraKeyMap is a std::map, and operator[] on a name it does not hold returns 0
(KEY_RESERVED). init() used four names that are not in pyraKeyMap.cpp:

- PYRA_KEY_PAUSE and PAUSE for Usr1 (KEY_PAUSE from the keypad), so Usr1 and
  Fn+Usr1 sent nothing. They are PYRA_KEY_USER1 and PYRA_KEY_FN_USR1.
- ESC for Fn+Esc, so Fn+Esc sent nothing instead of SysRq (PrtScrn). It is
  PYRA_KEY_FN_ESC.
- PYRA_KEY_RIGHT, which the map spells PYRA_KEY_RIFHT. D-pad right stayed a
  plain key and never moved the gamepad's ABS_HAT0X; left, up and down did.

The map also spells PYRA_KEY_LEFTAL for PYRA_KEY_LEFTALT. That one is left
alone: loadConfig() maps KEY_LEFTALT to the gamepad by its code, so Start
works, and fixing the name would make init() override an
altmode.right.trigger setting that moves left Alt to the right trigger.

mati found the first three names (Pyra forum, November 2025).

Against funkeymonkey-pyrainput 0.1.19 (applies with or without 0001 and 0002).
Apply with: patch -p1 < this-file

--- a/pyraKeyMap.cpp
+++ b/pyraKeyMap.cpp
@@ -8,7 +8,7 @@ std::map<std::string, int> pyraKeyMap = {
 {"PYRA_KEY_UP"				,	KEY_UP         },
 {"PYRA_KEY_DOWN"			,	KEY_DOWN       },
 {"PYRA_KEY_LEFT"			,	KEY_LEFT       },
-{"PYRA_KEY_RIFHT"			,	KEY_RIGHT      },
+{"PYRA_KEY_RIGHT"			,	KEY_RIGHT      },
 {"PYRA_KEY_LEFTAL"			,	KEY_LEFTALT    },
 {"PYRA_KEY_LEFTCTRL"		,	KEY_LEFTCTRL   },
 {"PYRA_KEY_HOME"			,	KEY_HOME       },
--- a/pyrainput.cpp
+++ b/pyrainput.cpp
@@ -70,8 +70,8 @@ void init(char const** argv, unsigned int argc) {
 		global.Fn.pressed = global.Fn.left || global.Fn.right;
 	});
 
-	global.behaviors->altmap(KEY_ESC,	&global.Fn.pressed, pyraKeyMap["PYRA_KEY_ESC"],	pyraKeyMap["ESC"]);
-	global.behaviors->altmap(KEY_PAUSE,	&global.Fn.pressed, pyraKeyMap["PYRA_KEY_PAUSE"],	pyraKeyMap["PAUSE"]);
+	global.behaviors->altmap(KEY_ESC,	&global.Fn.pressed, pyraKeyMap["PYRA_KEY_ESC"],	pyraKeyMap["PYRA_KEY_FN_ESC"]);
+	global.behaviors->altmap(KEY_PAUSE,	&global.Fn.pressed, pyraKeyMap["PYRA_KEY_USER1"],	pyraKeyMap["PYRA_KEY_FN_USR1"]);
         global.behaviors->complex(KEY_BRIGHTNESSUP, handleBrightness);
 	//global.behaviors->altmap(KEY_BRIGHTNESSUP,	&global.Fn.pressed, KEY_BRIGHTNESSUP,	KEY_BRIGHTNESSDOWN);
 	global.behaviors->altmap(KEY_F11,	&global.Fn.pressed, pyraKeyMap["PYRA_KEY_F11"],	pyraKeyMap["PYRA_KEY_FN_F11"]);
